<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28647" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mendēs</span></b> , ētis,
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mendēsīcus</span></b> ,
		and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mendēsĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to the
				Egyptian maritime town Mendes</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(a).</b> Mendes: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Asclepias,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 94</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b>
			Mendesicus: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ostium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					5, 10, 11, § 64</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(g).</b>
			Mendesius: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nomos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					5, 9, 9, § 49</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">unguentum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					13, 1, 2, § 17</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
